June (docs): Quick: we need a tiny troubleshooting snippet for 429s that may return partial responses. Keep it very short (one-paragraph + tiny JS example).

Ravi (sdk): Got it. Recommendation: message-level trimming, never drop system prompts, honor Retry-After >=1s else backoff. Short JS example coming.

Tess (eng-runtime): Runtime sets x-partial-ok when partial content was returned. Log that and avoid re-applying side effects until you reconcile.

Ravi (sdk): Snippet:
```js
// trim oldest non-system turns, retry on 429
async function safeSend(client, convo){
 for(let i=0;i<3;i++){
  try{return await client.generate({conversation:convo});}
  catch(e){
   if(e.status!==429) throw e;
   const ra=parseFloat(e.headers?.['retry-after']||'0');
   await sleep(ra>=1?ra*1000:Math.pow(2,i)*300);
   while(convo.length&&tokenCount(convo)>2500){ if(convo[0].role==='system')break; convo.shift(); }
  }
 }
 throw new Error('retries exhausted');
}
```

Lola (devex): I'll add two short localized strings after merge: 'Trying trimmed context...' and 'Retrying after backoff'.

